# Backend (Go)

- Stack is fixed (SPEC §2.1): chi router, pgx + sqlc (no ORM), goose migrations
  (embedded, run at startup), client-go, helm v3 libraries, go-containerregistry,
  Masterminds/semver.
- Decode Helm release Secrets with `helm.sh/helm/v3` libraries in memory; persist only
  chart name/version/repo metadata. Never shell out to `helm` or `kubectl`.
- Never request or use any Kubernetes write verb. Read-only by design.
- Kubeconfigs: AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest (key = `OMASTX_MASTER_KEY`), never returned
  by any API after upload, never logged.
- Queries live in `internal/store/queries/*.sql`; regenerate with `make sqlc` and commit
  the generated code under `internal/store/db/`. Schema changes are new goose migrations -
  never edit an applied migration.
- Errors: RFC 7807-style problem JSON `{code, title, detail}`; detail must state cause +
  next step per SPEC §4.6.
- API mutations require the CSRF token; sessions are HttpOnly `SameSite=Lax` cookies.
- Tests are table-driven; drift engine and tag-selection logic must keep ≥ 90% coverage.
  Every API mutation gets an integration test against dockerized Postgres.
- Keep the `ArtifactProvider` / `VersionResolver` interfaces exactly as SPEC §2.2; new
  package kinds must be addable without touching the scan orchestrator.
